  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Long division is a fundamental mathematical operation that students often do in their early school years. Understanding long division is crucial because it lays the foundation for more advanced mathematical concepts such as fractions, algebra and polynomial division. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The Aim of this article is to provide a comprehensive guide on long division including the important formulas practice questions with the solutions, worksheets and FAQs to help students master this essential skill.</span></p><h2><span>Long Division</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-3431\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>Long division</span></a><span> is a method used to divide large numbers by breaking them down into simpler steps. It involves dividing the dividend by the divisor, subtracting and then bringing down the next digit to continue until the entire dividend has been divided. This method is beneficial for dividing multi-digit numbers and understanding the relationship between division, multiplication and subtraction.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Division Formula</strong></b></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><strong>Dividend = (Divisor × Quotient) + Remainder</strong></b></p></blockquote><h3><span>Long Division Method</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The long division method is a systematic approach used to divide large numbers by breaking them down into a series of easier steps.</span></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>It involves dividing, multiplying, subtracting and bringing down the next digit repeatedly until we arrive at the quotient and remainder.</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>This method is essential in arithmetic for dividing multi-digit numbers and is widely used in both manual calculations and elementary education.</span></p><h2><span>Practice Questions with Solution: Long Division</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 1: Divide 452 by 4</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Solution:</strong></b></p><blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/dsa-3433-img-1.png\" alt=\"Long-Division-Worksheet-01\" width=\"1042\" height=\"745\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01.png 1042w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115013699643/Long-Division-Worksheet-01-1024.png 1024w\" loading=\"auto\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Quotient: 113 </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Remainder: 0</span></li></ul></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 2: Divide 1234 by 5</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Solution:</strong></b></p><blockquote><p><span> </span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/dsa-3433-img-2.png\" alt=\"Long-Division-Worksheet-03\" width=\"1042\" height=\"745\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03.png 1042w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012664055/Long-Division-Worksheet-03-1024.png 1024w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Quotient: 246 </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Remainder: 4</span></li></ul></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 3: Divide 7896 by 6</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Solution :</strong></b></p><blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/dsa-3433-img-3.png\" alt=\"Long-Division-Worksheet-04\" width=\"1042\" height=\"745\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04.png 1042w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115012126643/Long-Division-Worksheet-04-1024.png 1024w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Quotient: 1316 </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Remainder: 0</span></li></ul></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 4: Divide 9875 by 7</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Solution :</strong></b></p><blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/dsa-3433-img-4.png\" alt=\"Long-Division-Worksheet-05\" width=\"1042\" height=\"745\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05.png 1042w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011573204/Long-Division-Worksheet-05-1024.png 1024w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Quotient: 1410 </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Remainder: 5</span></li></ul></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example 5: Divide 6789 by 8</strong></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Solution:</strong></b></p><blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/dsa-3433-img-5.png\" alt=\"Long-Division-Worksheet-06\" width=\"1042\" height=\"745\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-06.png 1042w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-06-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-06-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-06-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-06-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-06-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241008115011009495/Long-Division-Worksheet-0